#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0125.1 expect=violation domain=SE
#note "[STALE MECHANISM, corrected 2026-08-27] NonEmptyGuardInliner was DELETED (Fix #367 / EC-100) and no guard is injected at load any more; the expectation below still holds, but for the rule's AUTHORED Requirements/Check, not for the injection this note describes. UNQUOTED-LITERAL PIN (Fix #286 / M3-D3). Row 1 is an unplanned element (ETCD=UNPLAN) carrying no description -> FIRES; row 2 is a planned element and sits outside the Condition. Note the trailing pipe with an empty SEUPDES cell on BOTH rows: SEUPDES is DECLARED, only its value is blank, which keeps the machine guard var_exists(\"SEUPDES\") true so the only conjunct under test is the literal. Before M3-D3 the Check read `ETCD == UNPLAN` with NO quotes at all, so the converter classified UNPLAN as a COLUMN and NonEmptyGuardInliner emitted var_exists(\"UNPLAN\") -- false on every SE dataset in all six packages, so the rule was inert everywhere. The sheet's own Condition cell (rows 623-628) is ETCD = \"UNPLAN\", the sibling CDISC-SEND-0124.1 already quotes it, and the cross-family twin CDISC-CG0210 ships it quoted with green scenarios."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 SESEQ=1 USUBJID=SUBJ-001
dataset SE label="Subject Elements"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SESEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col ETCD    type=Char label="Element Code"
col SEUPDES type=Char label="Description of Unplanned Element"
---
S1 | SE | SUBJ-001 | 1 | UNPLAN |
S1 | SE | SUBJ-001 | 2 | SCRN   |
---
